Subject: [PATCH] ufs: qcom: vote SM8475 CX and MX corners while scaling clocks

Use the existing UFS multi-clock OPP callback and GDSC parent performance
propagation. The locked OEM cape GCC driver requires LOW_SVS at 75 MHz
and TURBO_L1 at 850 MHz on both vdd_cx and vdd_mxa; the latter supply is
mx.lvl in all RPMh sets, not the distinct active-only MX_AO supply.

Scale ICE with AXI and UniPro so no independently enabled 300 MHz ICE
clock outlives a LOW_SVS request. Give ICE a 75 MHz bootstrap default and
its minimum active corner before its driver enables the clock. These
assigned rates are initial defaults; UFS continues to scale dynamically.

Keep each board timing compatible intact. Recognize 850 MHz as gear 4
only on SM8475 machines, including boards retaining the SM8450 timing.
Leave the SM8450 GCC domain count and UFS legacy path unchanged.

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -2583,6 +2583,10 @@
 	case 403000000:
 		gear = UFS_HS_G5;
 		break;
+	case 850000000:
+		if (!of_machine_is_compatible("qcom,sm8475"))
+			return UFS_HS_DONT_CHANGE;
+		fallthrough;
 	case 300000000:
 		gear = UFS_HS_G4;
 		break;
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,gcc-sm8450.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,gcc-sm8450.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,gcc-sm8450.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/qcom,gcc-sm8450.yaml
@@ -48,8 +48,10 @@
     minItems: 2
 
   power-domains:
+    minItems: 1
     items:
       - description: CX power domain
+      - description: MX power domain
 
 required:
   - compatible
@@ -60,6 +62,19 @@
 
 allOf:
   - $ref: qcom,gcc.yaml#
+
+  - if:
+      properties:
+        compatible:
+          const: qcom,sm8475-gcc
+    then:
+      properties:
+        power-domains:
+          minItems: 2
+    else:
+      properties:
+        power-domains:
+          maxItems: 1
 
 unevaluatedProperties: false
 
